  "notes": "child = 'EPSDT DENTAL PROGRAM' sheet (under 21); adult = 'ADULT DENTURE PROGRAM' sheet (only 6 codes: D0150, D0210, D5110, D5120, D5211, D5212 - general adults 21+ are covered for dentures only). Separate sheets exist for the ADULT WAIVER DENTAL PROGRAM (NOW/ROW waiver adults) and ADULT ICF/IID DENTAL PROGRAM, whose fees for the listed codes are identical to EPSDT; they were not recorded as 'adult'. Restoration codes D2140-D2394 have several rows (primary vs permanent teeth, surface combinations): the 'child' key is the first listed row (primary teeth), and each variant is recorded under child_<variant> keys exactly as listed. by_report: orthodontic D8070/D8080/D8090 show '***** Max Fee' (prior authorization and manual pricing): max fees printed {\"D8070\": \"***** Max Fee 4,182.00\", \"D8080\": \"***** Max Fee 4,281.00\", \"D8090\": \"***** Max Fee 4,515.00\"}. Per-row EFF DATE is mostly 20250421 (sedation codes 20260101; adult denture rows 20230830). Most Louisiana Medicaid dental benefits are administered by Dental Benefit Program Managers (MCNA, DentaQuest); this is the state fee-for-service schedule. Page lists '01/01/26 EXCEL' (this file) and a prior '10/15/25 EXCEL'.",
